{"version":1,"slug":"organized__Others__Reasoning__Coding-Decoding__Reasoning_-_Coding-Decoding_-_CODING_DECODING_(2)_(20Q)","path":"organized/Others/Reasoning/Coding-Decoding/Reasoning - Coding-Decoding - CODING DECODING (2) (20Q).html","title":"devgagan","provider":"organized","category":"Others/Reasoning/Coding-Decoding","durationMinutes":60,"totalQuestions":20,"sectionsLocked":false,"sections":null,"questions":[{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In a certain code language, 'electric wire circuit coal' is written as 'DB DA AK BC', 'gadget electric bulb' is written as 'US AK MP', 'light fan wire' is written as 'DB IM OZ' and 'coal bulb switch circuit' is written as 'BC DA UV US'. What is the code for 'switch' in the same language?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337; &#2349;&#2366;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, 'electric Wire Circuit Coal' &#2325;&#2379; 'DB DA AK BC', 'gadget electric Bulb' &#2325;&#2379; 'US AK MP', 'light fan Wire' &#2325;&#2379; 'DB IM OZ' &#2324;&#2352; 'coal Bulb Switch Circuit' &#2325;&#2379; 'BC DA UV US' &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360;&#2368; &#2349;&#2366;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 'switch' &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">DA</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">DA</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">BC</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">BC</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">US</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">US</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">UV</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">UV</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>It is given that, </p><p>'electric wire circuit coal' is written as 'DB DA AK BC' ------(I)</p><p>'gadget electric bulb' is written as 'US AK MP' -----(II)</p><p>'light fan wire' is written as 'DB IM OZ' ------(III)</p><p>'coal bulb switch circuit' is written as 'BC DA UV US' ----(IV)</p><p>From (I) and (IV), the code for 'coal circuit' is DA BC (in any order).</p><p>From (II) and (IV), the code for 'bulb' is US. </p><p>So, the remaining code i.e., UV will be the code for 'switch'. </p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In a certain coded language, 'Please go back' is coded as 'FGT KLO BCZ', 'Please shut the door' is coded as 'EJY PAS BCZ UQD' and 'The Back Window' is coded as 'UQD FGT RIN'. How will 'Shut' be coded in that language?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337;&#2367;&#2340; &#2349;&#2366;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, 'Please go back' &#2325;&#2379; 'FGT KLO BCZ' &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, 'Please closed the door' &#2325;&#2379; 'EJY PAS BCZ UQD' &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; 'The Back Window' &#2325;&#2379; 'UQD FGT RIN' &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360; &#2349;&#2366;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 'Shut' &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2376;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2327;&#2366;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">UQD</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">UQD</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">EJY</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">EJY</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">PAS</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">PAS</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Cannot be determined</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">Cannot be determined</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>'<b>Please</b> go <b>back</b>' is coded as '<b>FGT</b> KLO <b>BCZ</b>'</p><p>'<b>Please </b>shut <b>the</b> door' is coded as 'EJY PAS <b>BCZ UQD</b>'</p><p>'<b>The Back</b> Window' is coded as '<b>UQD FGT</b> RIN'</p><p>The code of 'Please' = BCZ</p><p>The code of 'Back' = FGT</p><p>The code of 'The' = UQD</p><p>Thus,</p><p>The code of 'Shut' / 'Door' = EJY / PAS</p><p>So, the answer is, 'cannot be determined'.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In certain code language  -  </p><p>'753' means 'Sit on table'</p><p>'159' means 'Stand on chair.'</p><p>'682' means 'four bed there'</p><p>Which of the following numbers stands for 'there' in that language?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337; &#2349;&#2366;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; - </p><p>'753' &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341; &#2361;&#2376; '&#2335;&#2375;&#2348;&#2354; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2376;&#2336;&#2379;'</p><p>'159' &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341; &#2361;&#2376; '&#2325;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2360;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352; &#2326;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2323;.'</p><p>'682' &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341; &#2361;&#2376; '&#2330;&#2366;&#2352; &#2348;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2352; &#2357;&#2361;&#2366;&#2305;'</p><p>&#2313;&#2360; &#2349;&#2366;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; '&#2357;&#2361;&#2366;&#2305;' &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">6</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">6</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">8<b> </b></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">8</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">2</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">5</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">5</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>The number that stands for 'there' in that language is '2'. </p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In a certain code language:</p><p>'G L O W' is written as '$% &amp;* &amp;~ @&gt;'</p><p>'W O L F' is written as '&amp;* @# $% @&gt;'</p><p>Which of the following can be the way in which 'F L O G' is written in that code language?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337; &#2349;&#2366;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;:</p><p>'G L O W' &#2325;&#2379; '$% &amp;* &amp;~ @&gt;' &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;</p><p>'W O L F' &#2325;&#2379; '&amp;* @# $% @&gt;' &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;</p><p>&#2313;&#2360; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337; &#2349;&#2366;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 'F L O G' &#2325;&#2379; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">@# @&gt; &amp;* &amp;~</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">@# @&gt; &amp;* &amp;~</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">@^ @&lt; &amp;* &amp;~</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">@^ @&lt; &amp;* &amp;~</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">@# @&gt; &amp;^ &amp;~</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">@# @&gt; &amp;^ &amp;~</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">@^ @&gt; &amp;* &amp;~</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">@^ @&gt; &amp;* &amp;~</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>The code for </p><p>L/O/W ---- &amp;*/ @&gt;/ $%</p><p>G --- &amp;~</p><p>F --- @#</p><p>So, the code for 'F L O G' will be '@# @&gt; &amp;* &amp;~' because in other options there are symbols that have not code value. </p><p>Thus, option (a) is the correct answer. </p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In a certain code language, 0402060205 means 'Ajit is father of Varun' and 0502110206 means 'Geeta is grandmother of Karuna'. Which of the following is the code for 'Girish is cousin of Pournima'?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337; &#2349;&#2366;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 0402060205 &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341; 'Ajit is father of Varun' &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; 0502110206 &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341; 'Geeta is grandmother of Karuna' &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344;-&#2360;&#2366; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354;&#2381;&#2346; 'Girish is cousin of Pournima' &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">0208060207</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">0208060207</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">0602020305</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">0602020305</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">0602060208</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">0602060208</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">0507090203</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">0507090203</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>0402060205 means 'Ajit is father of Varun' and 0502110206 means 'Geeta is grandmother of Karuna'</p><p>Thus, the pattern is:</p><p>The words are replaced by the total number of letters present in it.</p><p>If the letters present in the word is a single digit number, then 0 is written before it and if the letters present in the word is a double digit number, then it is written as it is.</p><p>Example: Ajit = 04 and grandmother = 11</p><p>So, Girish is cousin of Pournima= 0602060208</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In a certain code language 'Back to School' is written as '1#A 9%H 7@T', 'Stay in School' is written as '6&amp;Y 7@T 2*M' and 'Stay Back in Life' is written as '9%H 6&amp;Y 2*M 0$V'. How is 'Life' written in that code?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337; &#2349;&#2366;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 'Back to School' &#2325;&#2379; '1#A 9%H 7@T' &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, 'Stay in School' &#2325;&#2379; '6&amp;Y 7@T 2*M' &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; 'Stay Back in Life' &#2325;&#2379; '9%H 6&amp;Y 2*M 0$V' &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337; &#2349;&#2366;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 'Life' &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2376;&#2360;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2327;&#2366;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">2*M</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2*M</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">4!Q</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">4!Q</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">0$V</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">0$V</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Cannot be determined</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2344;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2340; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366;</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>'Back to School' is written as '1#A 9%H 7@T'</p><p>'Stay in School' is written as '6&amp;Y 7@T 2*M'</p><p>'Stay Back in Life' is written as '9%H 4!Q 2*M 0$V'</p><p>Code of 'Back' = '9%H'</p><p>Code of 'In/Stay' = '2*M/6&amp;Y'</p><p>Code of 'School' = '7@T'</p><p>Code of 'To' = '1#A' </p><p>Thus,</p><p>Code of 'Life' will be '0$V'</p><p>So, the answer is option (c).</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In a certain code language, 'Five foreign countries' means 'si po le', 'Countries at war' means 'ru ti po' and 'Turn at five' means 'ru ha si'. What is the code for the word 'Turn'?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337; &#2349;&#2366;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 'Five foreign countries' &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341; 'si po le' &#2361;&#2376;, 'Countries at war' &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341; 'ru ti po' &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; 'Turn at five' &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341; 'ru ha si' &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2358;&#2348;&#2381;&#2342; 'Turn' &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">le</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">le</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">ha</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">ha</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">ru</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">ru</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">si</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">si</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p><u>Five </u>foreign <b>countries</b> == <u>si </u><b>po</b> le</p><p><b>Countries</b> <s>at</s> war == <s>ru</s> ti <b>po</b></p><p>Turn <s>at </s><u>five</u> == <s>ru</s> ha <u>si</u></p><p>So, we get the codes as:</p><p>five = si</p><p>countries = po</p><p>foreign = le</p><p>at = ru</p><p>war = ti</p><p>turn = ha</p><p>Hence, the code for the word 'Turn' is 'ha'.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In a certain code language, 'past is history' is written 'tu su mu', 'present is mystery' is written as 'ku au tu' and 'past was present' is written as 'ru au su'. How will 'mystery' be written in that language? </p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337; &#2349;&#2366;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 'past is history' &#2325;&#2379; 'tu su mu' &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, 'present is mystery' &#2325;&#2379; 'ku au tu' &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; 'past was present' &#2325;&#2379; 'ru au su' &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2349;&#2366;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 'mystery' &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2327;&#2366;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">ku</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">ku</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">ru</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">ru</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">tu</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">tu</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">au</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">au</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>It is given that: </p><p>'past is history' is written 'tu su mu' -------I</p><p>'present is mystery' is written as 'ku au tu' -----II</p><p>'past was present' is written as 'ru au su' ------III</p><p>From I and II, 'is' is written as 'tu'.</p><p>From II and III, 'present' is written as 'au'.</p><p>So, the remaining 'mystery' is written as 'ku'. </p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In a certain code language, 'Love Your Job' is written as 'EB SB DB', 'Love And Enjoy' is written as 'EB GB LB' and 'Enjoy The Job' is written as 'SB LB NB'. How will 'Your' be written in that language?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337; &#2349;&#2366;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 'Love Your Job' &#2325;&#2379; 'EB SB DB' &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, 'Love And Enjoy' &#2325;&#2379; 'EB GB LB' &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; 'Enjoy The Job' &#2325;&#2379; 'SB LB NB' &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2349;&#2366;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 'Your' &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2327;&#2366;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">DB</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">DB</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">GB</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">GB</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">EB</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">EB</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">SB</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">SB</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p><b><img width=399 height=128 id=\"Picture 10\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20244/image011.jpg\" alt=1.png></b></p><p></p><p>Hence 'Your' will be written as DB.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In a certain code language, 'lets plant trees' is written as 'xy ab pq', 'to make earth green' is written as 'ef mn rs cd', 'green trees make air clean' is written as 'tu ij cd pq mn' and 'plant needs clean soil' is written as 'gh xy kl ij'. How will 'air' be written in that language?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337; &#2349;&#2366;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 'lets plant trees' &#2325;&#2379; 'xy ab pq' &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, 'to make earth green' &#2325;&#2379; 'ef mn rs cd' &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, 'green trees make air clean' &#2325;&#2379; 'tu ij cd pq mn' &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; 'plant needs clean soil' &#2325;&#2379; 'gh xy kl ij' &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2349;&#2366;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 'air' &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2327;&#2366;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">ij</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">ij</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">pq</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">pq</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">tu</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">tu</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">mn</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">mn</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>'lets plant trees' is written as 'xy ab pq' ------I</p><p>'to make earth green' is written as 'ef mn rs cd' ------II</p><p>'green trees make air clean' is written as 'tu ij cd pq mn' ----III</p><p>'plant needs clean soil' is written as 'gh xy kl ij' ------IV</p><p>From II and III, green make is written as mn cd (in any order).</p><p>From I and III, trees is written as pq.</p><p>From III and IV, clean is written as ij.</p><p>So, air will be written as tu.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In a coded language, \"find that bag\" is coded as \"359\", \"that is good\" is coded as \"136\" , \"is it here\" is coded as \"860\" and \"bag is good\" is coded as \"961\". Select the option which shows the correct code.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337;&#2367;&#2340; &#2349;&#2366;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; \"find that bag\" &#2325;&#2379; \"359\" &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, \"that is good\" &#2325;&#2379; \"136\" &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, \"is it here\" &#2325;&#2379; \"860\" &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; \"bag is good\" &#2325;&#2379; \"961\"&#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354;&#2381;&#2346; &#2325;&#2366; &#2330;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; &#2332;&#2379; &#2360;&#2361;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">good - 3</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">good - 3</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">is - 6</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">is - 6</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">find - 9</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">find - 9</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">bag - 1</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">bag - 1</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>It is given that,</p><p>\"find that bag\" is coded as \"359\" ......................(1)</p><p>\"that is good\" is coded as \"136\" .......................(2)</p><p>\"bag is good\" is coded as \"961\" ........................(3)</p><p>\"is it here\" is coded as \"860\" .............................(4)</p><p>From (1) and (2), that == 3.</p><p>From (1) and (3), bag == 9.</p><p>From (2), (3) and (4), is == 6.</p><p>From (1), find == 5.</p><p>From (2), good == 1.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In a certain code language, 'Climb the trees' is coded as 'bet get jet', 'Trees give peace' is coded as 'get let net' and 'The peace within' is coded as 'let bet pet'. How will 'Climb' be written in that language?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337; &#2349;&#2366;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, 'Climb the trees' &#2325;&#2379; 'bet get jet' &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, 'Trees give peace' &#2325;&#2379; 'get let net' &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; 'The peace within' &#2325;&#2379; 'let bet pet' &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2349;&#2366;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 'Climb' &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2376;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2327;&#2366;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Get</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">Get</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Bet</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">Bet</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Pet</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">Pet</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Jet</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">Jet</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>'Climb <b>the trees</b>' is coded as '<b>bet get</b> jet'</p><p>'<b>Trees</b> give peace' is coded as '<b>get</b> let net'</p><p>'<b>The</b> peace within' is coded as 'let <b>bet</b> pet'</p><p>The code of 'the' = bet</p><p>The code of 'Trees' = get</p><p>Thus, the code for 'Climb' = jet</p><p>Thus, the answer is option (d).</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In a certain code language, 'Life is short' is coded as 'r@1 t$8 u&amp;2', 'Good in life' is coded as 'y*9 u&amp;2 m#7' and 'Good man is something is coded as 't$8 m#7 k~3 z^4'. How will 'Something' be coded in that language?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337; &#2349;&#2366;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, 'Life is short' &#2325;&#2379; 'r@1 t$8 u&amp;2' &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, 'Good in life' &#2325;&#2379; 'y*9 u&amp;2 m#7' &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; 'Good man is something' &#2325;&#2379; 't$8 m#7 k~3 z^4' &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2349;&#2366;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 'Something' &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2351;&#2375;&#2327;&#2366;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">t$8</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">t$8</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">k~3</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">k~3</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">z^4</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">z^4</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Cannot be determined</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2344;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2340; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366;</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>'<b>Life is</b> short' is coded as 'r@1 <b>t$8 u&amp;2'</b></p><p>'<b>Good</b> in <b>life</b>' is coded as 'y*9 <b>u&amp;2 m#7'</b></p><p>'<b>Good</b> man <b>is</b> something is coded as '<b>t$8 m#7</b> k~3 z^4'</p><p>The code for 'Life' = u&amp;2</p><p>The code for 'Is' = t$8</p><p>The code for 'Good' = m#7</p><p>Thus, the code for 'Something' is either 'k~3' or 'z^4'</p><p>Hence, the answer is cannot be determined.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In certain code language, \"Money Market Profit\" is coded as \"Ise Mse Fse\", \"Market Inflation Loss\" is coded as \"Mse Gse Tse\" and \"Market Profit Inflation\" is coded as \"Mse Fse Tse\", then find the code for \"Loss\".</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337; &#2349;&#2366;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, \"Money Market Profit\" &#2325;&#2379; \"Ise Mse Fse\" &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, \"Market Inflation Loss\" &#2325;&#2379; \"Mse Gse Tse\" &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; \"Market Profit Inflation\" &#2325;&#2379; \"Mse Fse Tse\" &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; \"Loss\" &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Tse</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">Tse</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Gse</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">Gse</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Mse</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">Mse</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Cannot be determined</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2344;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2340; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>In given code language,</p><p>\"Money <u>Market</u> Profit\" is coded as \"Ise <u>Mse</u> Fse\" .. (I)</p><p>\"<u>Market</u> <b>Inflation</b> Loss\" is coded as \"<u>Mse</u> Gse <b>Tse</b>\" .. (II)</p><p>\"<u>Market</u> Profit <b>Inflation</b>\" is coded as \"<u>Mse</u> Fse <b>Tse</b>\" .. (III)</p><p>From (I), (II) and (III): -</p><p>Market = Mse</p><p>From (II) and (III): -</p><p>Inflation = Tse</p><p>So,</p><p>\"Loss\" is coded as \"Gse\".</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In a certain code language, 'A' is written as 'H', 'C' is written as 'O', 'H' is written as 'N', 'M' is written as 'R', 'N' is written as 'A', 'O' is written as 'M' and 'R' is written as 'C'. How will 'NOMARCH' be written in the same code language?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337; &#2349;&#2366;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, 'A' &#2325;&#2379; 'H' &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, 'C' &#2325;&#2379; 'O' &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, 'H' &#2325;&#2379; 'N' &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, 'M' &#2325;&#2379; 'R' &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, 'N' &#2325;&#2379; 'A' &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, 'O' &#2325;&#2379; 'M' &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; 'R' &#2325;&#2379; 'C' &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337; &#2349;&#2366;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 'NOMARCH' &#2325;&#2376;&#2360;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2327;&#2366;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">HCONMRA</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">HCONMRA</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">AMRHCON</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">AMRHCON</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">RONMCHA</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">RONMCHA</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">MRACNOH</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">MRACNOH</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>Code</b></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">A</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">C</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">H</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">M</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">N</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">O</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">R</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>Original letters</b></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">H</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">O</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">N</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">R</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">A</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">M</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">C</td></tr></table></p><p>Hence, the code is AMRHCON.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In a certain code language, 'Stay positive and happy' is coded as '1*1 6@6 3!3 9&amp;9', 'With positive energy' is coded as '3!3 2%2 8$8' and 'Force and Energy' is coded as '2%2 7#7 6@6'. What is the code for 'Happy' in this code language?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2367;&#2358;&#2367;&#2359;&#2381;&#2335; &#2325;&#2370;&#2335; &#2349;&#2366;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, 'Stay positive and happy' &#2325;&#2379; '1*1 6@6 3!3 9&amp;9', 'With positive energy' &#2325;&#2379; '3!3 2%2 8$8' &#2324;&#2352; 'Force and Energy' &#2325;&#2379; '2%2 7#7 6@6' &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360; &#2325;&#2370;&#2335; &#2349;&#2366;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 'Happy' &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">9&amp;9</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">9&amp;9</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">8$8</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">8$8</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1*1</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1*1</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Either a or c</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2351;&#2366; &#2340;&#2379; a &#2351;&#2366; c</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>'Stay positive and happy' is coded as '1*1 6@6 3!3 9&amp;9'</p><p>'With positive energy' is coded as '3!3 2%2 8$8'</p><p>'Force and Energy' is coded as '2%2 7#7 6@6'</p><p>The code for 'Positive' = 3!3</p><p>The code for 'And' = 6@6</p><p>Thus,</p><p>The code for 'Happy' is either 1*1 or 9&amp;9</p><p>Thus, the answer is option (d).</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In a certain language, 'come go went' is written as 'P# U! R%', 'best good better' is written as 'T&amp; W@ S$', 'good time to come' is written as 'Q* T&amp; V^ R%' and 'better to go' is written as 'W@ P# Q*'. How 'time' will be written in that language?</p><p>I. Q*</p><p>II. V^</p><p>III. Either W@ or T&amp;</p><p>IV. R%</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2349;&#2366;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, 'come go went' &#2325;&#2379; 'P# U! R%' &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, 'best good better' &#2325;&#2379; 'T&amp; W@ S$' &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, 'good time to come' &#2325;&#2379; 'Q* T&amp; V^ R%' &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; 'better to go' &#2325;&#2379; 'W@ P# Q*' &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2349;&#2366;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 'time' &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2327;&#2366;?</p><p>I. Q*</p><p>II. V^</p><p>III. &#2351;&#2366; &#2340;&#2379; W@ &#2351;&#2366; T&amp;</p><p>IV. R%</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Only I</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; I</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Only II</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; II</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Either I or IV</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2351;&#2366; &#2340;&#2379; I &#2351;&#2366; IV</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Only III</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; III</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>'come go went' is written as 'P# U! R%'------I</p><p>'best good better' is written as 'T&amp; W@ S$'----II</p><p>'good time to come' is written as 'Q* T&amp; V^ R%'-----III</p><p>'better to go' is written as 'W@ P# Q*'-----IV</p><p>From I and III, come is written as R%. </p><p>From II and III, good is written as T&amp;.</p><p>From III and IV, to is written as Q*.</p><p>So, time will be written as V^. </p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In a certain language, 'no picture is released' is coded as 'cr mp am xy', 'her beautiful picture' is coded as 'ky sj mp' and 'no ugly is beautiful' is coded as 'sj cr rp xy' then 'cr' is the code for which word?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2349;&#2366;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, 'no picture is released' &#2325;&#2379; 'cr mp am xy' &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, 'her beautiful picture' &#2325;&#2379; 'ky sj mp' &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; 'no ugly is beautiful' &#2325;&#2379; 'sj cr rp xy' &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; 'cr' &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2358;&#2348;&#2381;&#2342; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">picture</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">picture</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">no</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">no</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">is</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">is</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Either is or no</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2351;&#2366; &#2340;&#2379; is &#2351;&#2366; no</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>'no picture is released' &#8594; 'cr mp am xy' .. (i)</p><p>'her beautiful picture' &#8594; 'ky sj mp' .. (ii)</p><p>'no ugly is beautiful' &#8594; 'sj cr rp xy' .. (iii)</p><p>From (i) and (ii)</p><p>Picture &#8594; mp</p><p>From (i) and (iii),</p><p>No/ is &#8594; cr/ xy</p><p>Hence, 'cr' is the code for either 'no' or 'is'.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Read the given information and answer the question(s) that follow(s).</p><p>In certain code language, 'TABLE CHAIR SIT' is written as 'OPT GET DIG', 'TWO PEOPLE CHAIR' is written as 'DIG HOT FOG'and 'TWO TABLE COVER' is written as 'FOG OPT JET'. How will 'SIT' be written in that language?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2360;&#2370;&#2330;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2397;&#2367;&#2319; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2310;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2358;&#2381;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2352; &#2342;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337; &#2349;&#2366;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, 'TABLE CHAIR SIT' &#2325;&#2379; 'OPT GET DIG' &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, 'TWO PEOPLE CHAIR' &#2325;&#2379; 'DIG HOT FOG' &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; 'TWO TABLE COVER' &#2325;&#2379; 'FOG OPT JET' &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2349;&#2366;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 'SIT' &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2327;&#2366;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">JET</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">JET</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">OPT</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">OPT</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">HOT</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">HOT</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">GET</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">GET</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p><b><img width=399 height=117 id=\"Picture 26\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20440/image026.png\" alt=1.png></b></p><p>So, </p><p>TABLE ---- OPT</p><p>CHAIR ---- DIG</p><p>SIT ---- GET</p><p>TWO ---- FOG</p><p>PEOPLE ---- HOT</p><p>COVER ---- JET</p><p>So, the code for 'SIT' is 'GET'.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In a certain code language, 'gear up skills' is written as 'H8 E5 A1', 'learn soft skills' is written as 'B4 F3 H8' and 'learn communicate conquer' is written as 'D2 F3 G7'. What among the following can be the possible code for 'soft conquer' in that language? </p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337; &#2349;&#2366;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 'gear up skills' &#2325;&#2379; 'H8 E5 A1' &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, 'learn soft skills' &#2325;&#2379; 'B4 F3 H8' &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; 'learn communicate conquer' &#2325;&#2379; 'D2 F3 G7' &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344;-&#2360;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2349;&#2366;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 'soft conquer' &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2360;&#2306;&#2349;&#2366;&#2357;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337; &#2361;&#2379; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">B4 F3</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">B4 F3</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">H8 D2</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">H8 D2</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">B4 D2</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">B4 D2</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">G7 F3</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">G7 F3</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>'gear up skills' is written as 'H8 E5 A1'------I</p><p>'learn soft skills' is written as 'B4 F3 H8'-----II</p><p>'learn communicate conquer' is written as 'D2 F3 G7' -----III</p><p>From I and II, skills is written as H8. </p><p>From II and III, learn is written as F3. </p><p>So, soft is written as B4.</p><p>And 'communicate conquer' is written as 'D2 G7' (in any order). </p><p>So, the code for 'soft conquer' is 'B4 D2' or 'B4 G7'. </p>","marks":2,"section":null}]}